course: dictionary
lesson: 9510
title: Looking after what we are given
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A steward is someone who looks after something for someone else, or for the future. Stewardship is the care they give: the job of looking after things carefully. You can see the word steward inside it, and that is a clue.
explain: «God gives people the job of caring for the animals and the land; this is called stewardship.» Here stewardship means the duty to look after the earth and its animals, and not waste them. Read the sentence and ask: who is looking after what, and for whom?
explain: Stewardship is also used about money and businesses. «Good stewardship» means managing money carefully and responsibly, saving it wisely instead of spending it all. The words around it show which meaning is being used: the land and animals point one way, and money points another.
fact: Stewardship is a noun, so it names a job or a way of caring.
fact: A steward is someone who looks after things that belong to someone else, or that must last for the future.
fact: «Stewardship of the earth» means caring for the planet, for example by recycling, saving energy and protecting animals.
fact: «Good stewardship» means managing things, such as money or time, carefully and wisely.
fact: Christians believe God gave people stewardship of the world, meaning the duty to care for it and not waste it.
exercise: «God gives people the job of caring for the animals and the land; this is called stewardship.» What is stewardship in this sentence? | *Looking after the animals and land carefully | Owning as many animals and as much land as you can | Playing outside all day | Selling the land for money
exercise: Which action shows good stewardship of the earth? | Dropping litter in the park because someone else will pick it up | *Turning off the lights when you leave a room | Leaving the tap running while you brush your teeth
exercise: «The school garden grew well under the stewardship of Mrs Okafor.» What does under the stewardship of mean here? | *Looked after by | Hidden from | Painted by | Paid for by the parents
test: Which is an example of good stewardship of money? | Spending it all on sweets the day you get it | Lending it to a friend and forgetting who | *Saving some of your pocket money each week | Hiding it under the bed and never checking
test: What does stewardship mean in «Christians believe God gave people stewardship of the world»? | Owning the world and doing whatever you like | *The duty to care for the world and not waste it | Making as much noise in the world as possible | Having nothing to do with the world
exam: Which word names the careful care of something entrusted to you? | *Stewardship | Neglect | Wastefulness | Carelessness
